{:task "seon.context/similar-finds-helpers-by-embedding" :merge "3bf931bca" :plan-at "parent" :plan "What exists: the context's `:found` names helpers by the call graph (`seon.context/found`), which finds a helper something already calls; `my.program/search` and `similar` are missing (docs/parity.md#the-agents-repl-my). The ruling is DECISIONS \"Embeddings join the context\": fused, small and measured. Earlier work exists only outside this repository: `~/src/seon-jolt/em1` (a brute-force kNN in C, `knn.c` and `csrc/proto_knn.c`, 10k x 768 in 0.39 ms; the embed service in `server` and `src`; `patches/agents-01-embed.patch` and `core-01-embed.patch`; measurements and the R@10 corpus in `out/`), recorded in the outer repository's notes/archive/option3-EM1-embeddings.md; R4 measured the lever: 7/32 green without helper naming, 22/24 with. What correct looks like: an embedding per program function kept with its form, a kNN over them through the effect owner, `similar` at the REPL and the top hits beside `:found` in the context, each measured (recall on the corpus, cost per context build). Model downloads are an open owner question (RESUME)." :fns ["my.agent/similar" "seon.context/current-state" "seon.context/found" "seon.context/rrf" "seon.fx/admit" "seon.fx/batch" "seon.fx/charge" "seon.fx/dispatch" "seon.fx/outcome" "seon.fx/owner-proc" "seon.fx/procs" "seon.fx/reply!" "seon.fx/spent?" "seon.fx/worker-proc" "seon.proofs/check-steps" "seon.root/start!" "seon.schema.datahike/type->datahike" "seon.system/build-fx" "seon.vector/document-prompt" "seon.vector/due" "seon.vector/embed" "seon.vector/embed-texts" "seon.vector/model-id" "seon.vector/near" "seon.vector/open" "seon.vector/pack" "seon.vector/pack-dims" "seon.vector/query-prompt" "seon.vector/round" "seon.vector/stored" "seon.vector/texts" "seon.vector/tx-data" "seon.vector/unpack" "seon.vector/vector-of" "seon.vector/vectors-proc"] :sections ["docs/README.md#the-running-system" "docs/decisions.md#embeddings-join-the